  "worked_solution": "To compute ${f}^{\u2032}(1.5),$ we need to find the slope of the tangent to $f(x)$ at $x=1.5.$\n\nLet's consider the graph of $y=f(x)$ for $x\\in [-1,3].$ Notice that $x=1.5$ lies in this interval.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/assets/56cb6eb057efc5bf73e92fea0a78bacdf4bdd1ac43fdd28b23b08bbbbdff346c.png)\n\nThe slope of $y=f(x)$ on $x\\in (-1,3)$ is constant and equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u0394f}{\u0394x} & =\\frac{0-2}{3-(-1)}=\\frac{-2}{4}=-0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{\u2032}(1.5)=-0.5.$",
